1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:03,073
Day one.

2
00:00:03,633 --> 00:00:04,875
Six students.

3
00:00:04,835 --> 00:00:06,553
Three million dong each.

4
00:00:07,313 --> 00:00:09,031
Thirty days to survive.

5
00:00:10,131 --> 00:00:11,564
Let's see how that goes.

6
00:00:17,467 --> 00:00:19,314
Ray: Bubble tea for everyone!

7
00:00:19,274 --> 00:00:20,426
Ray: It's on me!

8
00:00:22,526 --> 00:00:24,399
Day one, Ray was a king.

9
00:00:25,959 --> 00:00:28,820
Day five, Ray was eating instant noodles.

10
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:33,117
Day six… also instant noodles.

11
00:00:40,733 --> 00:00:42,683
Pia: It was seventy percent off!

12
00:00:42,643 --> 00:00:44,639
Pia: I basically made money!

13
00:00:47,139 --> 00:00:48,595
Pia doesn't own a duck.

14
00:00:49,155 --> 00:00:50,885
Pia doesn't need a duck lamp.

15
00:00:51,645 --> 00:00:53,197
But Pia "saved" money.

16
00:00:53,497 --> 00:00:54,692
Seven times.

17
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:02,378
Bea: It's not spending.

18
00:01:02,338 --> 00:01:04,296
Bea: It's investing in myself.

19
00:01:06,796 --> 00:01:08,645
Courses opened: zero.

20
00:01:09,405 --> 00:01:11,016
Gym visits: one.

21
00:01:11,916 --> 00:01:13,706
To take a selfie in the mirror.

22
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:23,021
Yuki: I never check my balance.

23
00:01:22,981 --> 00:01:25,688
Yuki: If I don't look, it can't hurt me.

24
00:01:28,188 --> 00:01:29,133
Day twenty.

25
00:01:29,693 --> 00:01:30,709
Yuki looked.

26
00:01:32,209 --> 00:01:33,130
It hurt.

27
00:01:39,533 --> 00:01:41,851
Otto: Bro… can I borrow fifty?

28
00:01:41,811 --> 00:01:43,860
Otto: I'll pay you back next month.

29
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:44,999
Otto: Probably.

30
00:01:46,699 --> 00:01:48,072
Otto never has money.

31
00:01:49,372 --> 00:01:52,305
Somehow, Otto has the best phone in the building.

32
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,603
Gus: Two thousand dong for parking?

33
00:02:01,563 --> 00:02:02,824
Gus: No way.

34
00:02:02,784 --> 00:02:03,973
Gus: I'll walk.

35
00:02:03,933 --> 00:02:05,603
Gus: Five kilometers.

36
00:02:07,303 --> 00:02:09,926
Gus has a spreadsheet to track his spreadsheets.

37
00:02:09,886 --> 00:02:11,759
Richest student in the building.

38
00:02:12,059 --> 00:02:13,480
Also the most tired.

39
00:02:19,267 --> 00:02:20,295
Day thirty.

40
00:02:20,255 --> 00:02:22,092
Six different spending styles.

41
00:02:22,852 --> 00:02:23,808
Same ending.

42
00:02:23,768 --> 00:02:27,593
Here's the trick: save a little first, then spend what's left.

43
00:02:29,493 --> 00:02:32,745
Ray: So… who's treating bubble tea next month?
